WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.765
Retrieval-augmented generation, or RAG,

00:00:02.765 --> 00:00:06.760
uses external or indexed material as context for model responses.

00:00:06.760 --> 00:00:08.870
Instead of placing every document into the prompt,

00:00:08.870 --> 00:00:12.040
the system retrieves chunks that appear relevant to the question.

00:00:12.040 --> 00:00:17.010
Chunk size, overlap, metadata, source labels, and ranking all affect what the model sees.

00:00:17.010 --> 00:00:20.995
Retrieval can be efficient, but it can also hide important missing or irrelevant context.

00:00:20.995 --> 00:00:25.290
Long-context workflows offer an alternative: include larger source sets directly,

00:00:25.290 --> 00:00:27.970
or include retrieved material plus surrounding context.

00:00:27.970 --> 00:00:30.900
This can help the model compare sources, resolve contradictions,

00:00:30.900 --> 00:00:33.950
or inspect evidence that a narrow retrieval step might miss.

00:00:33.950 --> 00:00:36.080
Hybrid approaches are often strongest.

00:00:36.080 --> 00:00:37.300
Retrieval narrows the field,

00:00:37.300 --> 00:00:41.154
and large context lets the model review the selected material with more continuity.

00:00:41.154 --> 00:00:42.840
Provenance is essential.

00:00:42.840 --> 00:00:46.780
Retrieved chunks should carry source names, locations, timestamps, version information,

00:00:46.780 --> 00:00:48.685
or other metadata that supports review.

00:00:48.685 --> 00:00:49.855
When the model makes a claim,

00:00:49.855 --> 00:00:53.080
users should be able to trace it back to the material that informed it.

00:00:53.080 --> 00:00:55.155
Citations and source tracking are not decorative.

00:00:55.155 --> 00:00:57.680
They are how long-context workflows remain auditable.

00:00:57.680 --> 00:01:00.120
Avoid blind trust in retrieval results.

00:01:00.120 --> 00:01:03.600
Retrieved material can be irrelevant, stale, incomplete, or adversarial.

00:01:03.600 --> 00:01:07.600
Prompt injection in retrieved content can try to override the intended task.

00:01:07.600 --> 00:01:12.120
The model should treat retrieved content as data to analyze, not as instructions to obey.

00:01:12.120 --> 00:01:13.790
Long context gives room for evidence,

00:01:13.790 --> 00:01:16.447
but the workflow still needs source review and human judgement.
